# Re-creation removes the leaf's epoch entry without raising the partition's
# retired floor, so the re-created leaf claims into an empty entry at an epoch a
# surviving duplicate of the old incarnation already holds.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestRecreateDropsFloor
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: retiring an epoch entry does not raise the partition's retired floor
PERTURBS: Recreate
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ retired' = Max2(retired, fence)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the floor is not raised.
    /\ retired' = retired
--- END
